        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This adds Trusted Type info for a number of API. I am working of Firefox. Where possible I have attempted to determine Chrome and Safari data. Where not found I have marked as false. Supporting data for each case linked inline.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">APIs added</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/SVGAnimatedString/baseVal\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">SVGAnimatedString.baseVal</code></a> - TrustedScriptURL</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/WorkerGlobalScope/importScripts\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">WorkerGlobalScope.importScripts()</code></a> - TrustedScriptURL</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/ServiceWorkerContainer/register\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">ServiceWorkerContainer.register()</code></a> - TrustedScriptURL</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Content-Security-Policy/trusted-types\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">Content-Security-Policy: trusted-types</code></a> - support for setting the allowed trusted type policy names</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27836",
            "title": "Trusted type support updates for various APIs",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-12T07:13:07.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-12T04:23:19.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Addresses the dev-docs-needed requirement of <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1986688\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bug 1986688</a> Cookies are returned with a fractional expirationDate for the change made in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1972757\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bug 1972757</a> Store cookie expiry value as msec.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related MDN changes in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3404268110\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/41097\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/41097/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41097\">mdn/content#41097</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27833",
            "title": "Bug-1986688 Cookies expirationDate includes milliseconds",
            "date_modified": "2025-09-11T19:13:08.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-09-11T18:56:51.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "rebloor",
                "url": "https://github.com/rebloor"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/349114?u=1185d4fc45f5ff4c4a592b30a4dd2bb5cd1b7128&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">I don't think we need this sub feature.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The method itself has the same compatibility data. This new behavior might have come late but it shipped at the same time as the method itself. The spec for <code class=\"notranslate\">setReportEventDataForAutomaticBeacons</code> describes the behavior already.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27831",
            "title": "Remove Fence.setReportEventDataForAutomaticBeacons.start_commit_event…",
