        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7352080?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">As noted in the <a href=\"https://developer.chrome.com/blog/extension-news-october-2024#upcoming_features\" rel=\"nofollow\">Chrome Developers blog post</a>, support is provided for <code class=\"notranslate\">use_dynamic_url</code> in Chrome 130.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #23454.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2362815519\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/23454\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/23454/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/23454\">#23454</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27765",
            "title": "Issue-23454 webextensions.manifest.web_accessible_resources use_dynamic_url fully supported in Chrome",
